{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1016420-communing-with-spirits","id":1016420,"title":"Communing with spirits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-12T23:13:51-08:00","id":1016420,"title":"Communing with spirits","content":"So I have just finished a deep absorption of CB20, and the following has occurred to me - Ajaba, Corax, Kitsune, Gurahl, Nuwisha, Mokole, Ratkin, Camazotz, Grondr, members of the Ahadi and the Beast Courts all have access to the Gift 'Spirit Speech' (all at level 1, some only in factions within the breed, though for some reason Kitsune are the exception and get access at Rank 2). So how do Ananasi, Bastet, Nagah, Rokea and Apis commune with spirits? My ST is puzzled and cannot find an answer, so these breeds are all getting the Gift on their general lists at Level 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T03:10:04-08:00","id":1016966,"title":"","content":"I guess there is no clarity on this, as I suspected. It seems to be a strange oversight in that case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T10:04:53-08:00","id":1017125,"title":"","content":"I've never played in an all-X game where X is not Werewolf, so I really have no idea how that would work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T10:55:18-08:00","id":1017154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1016420-communing-with-spirits?p=1017125#post1017125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never played in an all-X game where X is not Werewolf, so I really have no idea how that would work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same.<br /> <br /> Your solution of making the gift universal sounds like a fine fix. Do what works best for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T11:57:26-08:00","id":1017195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>deejay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1016420-communing-with-spirits#post1016420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I have just finished a deep absorption of CB20, and the following has occurred to me - Ajaba, Corax, Kitsune, Gurahl, Nuwisha, Mokole, Ratkin, Camazotz, Grondr, members of the Ahadi and the Beast Courts all have access to the Gift 'Spirit Speech' (all at level 1, some only in factions within the breed, though for some reason Kitsune are the exception and get access at Rank 2). So how do Ananasi, Bastet, Nagah, Rokea and Apis commune with spirits? My ST is puzzled and cannot find an answer, so these breeds are all getting the Gift on their general lists at Level 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>Off the top of my head:<br /> Ananasi don't <i>need</i> to speak to spirits. They get their Gifts directly from Ananasa (via their seelie)<br /> Bastest can and do teach each other Gifts. And can steal the Gift Spirit Speech from another Fera. They also learn Gifts from Jamak.<br /> Nagah might be similar to the Ananasi, learning Gifts from the Wani.<br /> Rokea, if I remember correctly, just talk to Spirits since in the Ocean the Gauntlet is different. Remora are spirits that work with the Rokea without the need for a Gift. And Rorqual can assist them as well.<br /> <br /> No idea about the Apis<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T02:33:35-08:00","id":1017552,"title":"","content":"Thanks, interesting. I am not convinced the Ananasi or Nagah do not need to commune with spirits though. Spirits roles in WtA involve far more than just being fonts of Gifts. It seems pretty important given the Ananasi work with the Symmetry for ex (although they have Gifts that make certain spirits ignore them, that's not the same as communing). Aside from in character need, there is also player need. Many players of these breeds will want to interact with spirits, and should be able to, Great call on Bastet though, that is a genuine alternate way. And another good catch on Rokea, who do indeed get free communication, but not because of the different Gauntlet, but through Sending. So for now I am just assigning this Gift as a level 1 general Gift for Ananasi, Nagah and Apis, for player agency. Very interesting that Gaia seems to expect Bastet to steal Spirit Speech or learn it from Jamak, though. Could be a cool story there. I'd still like to know if the omission of Spirit Speech is a design choice or an oversight, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","user":"deejay","date":". 12-15-2016, 05:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T07:10:30-08:00","id":1017635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1016420-communing-with-spirits?p=1017195#post1017195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Off the top of my head:<br /> Ananasi don't <i>need</i> to speak to spirits. They get their Gifts directly from Ananasa (via their seelie)<br /> Bastest can and do teach each other Gifts. And can steal the Gift Spirit Speech from another Fera. They also learn Gifts from Jamak.<br /> Nagah might be similar to the Ananasi, learning Gifts from the Wani.<br /> Rokea, if I remember correctly, just talk to Spirits since in the Ocean the Gauntlet is different. Remora are spirits that work with the Rokea without the need for a Gift. And Rorqual can assist them as well.<br /> <br /> No idea about the Apis<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIn the breedbook for Nagah and Ananasi both were said to learn gifts from there patrons. In fact the Nagah are not part of the pact with the spirits the only spirits they learn gifts from are the Wani and their servants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T22:16:34-08:00","id":1017962,"title":"","content":"Aren't spirits able to understand and communicate in human speech, even if some might pretend they can't to avoid talking to people they're not fond of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T22:43:21-08:00","id":1017973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>deejay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1016420-communing-with-spirits?p=1017552#post1017552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits roles in WtA involve far more than just being fonts of Gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhhhhh... So, my $.02 is that <i>yes</i>, that<i> is </i>true -- but the same does not <i>necessarily</i> hold as true for the shapeshifters. One of the Gurahl is explaining why it's so much harder for the werebears to step sideways in the old Gurahl tribebook, and basically says that when Gaia created the Gurahl, She intended for them to be much more focused on the physical plane than the spiritual one. That basic concept tends to get brought up and reinforced every now and then in various other publications. Basically, it's the Garou, Corax and Nuwisha who are supposed to be <i>really</i> heavily focused on spirit-stuff (and even with the Nuwisha, it's hinted that that wasn't originally intended, but rather mission-creep stemming from the Nuwisha tendency to stick their noses in <i>everything</i> they can).<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't spirits able to understand and communicate in human speech, even if some might pretend they can't to avoid talking to people they're not fond of?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSometimes. The rule of thumb is that if a spirit is an urban spirit, it will generally know the local human dialect (or dialects, plural, if the area is highly multilingual). Or if the spirit is associated with a specific culture, it will generally know that culture's language (example: American Dream will definitely know English -- but may get thrown if you use certain words like &quot;petrol&quot; instead of &quot;gas&quot; or &quot;lift&quot; instead of &quot;elevator&quot;. Alternately Kwakwadjec (Wolverine) will probably know any of the American Indian tribal languages of tribes that historically communed with him -- with the quirk of knowing the &quot;dead&quot; languages of obscure tribes that no longer speak them, while remaining ignorant of major tribal languages -- like Navajo or Cherokee -- who never held him in their spiritual pantheon).<br /> <br /> Most other spirits will generally not know human languages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T01:58:38-08:00","id":1018001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1016420-communing-with-spirits?p=1017973#post1017973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ehhhhhh... So, my $.02 is that <i>yes</i>, that<i> is </i>true -- but the same does not <i>necessarily</i> hold as true for the shapeshifters. One of the Gurahl is explaining why it's so much harder for the werebears to step sideways in the old Gurahl tribebook, and basically says that when Gaia created the Gurahl, She intended for them to be much more focused on the physical plane than the spiritual one. That basic concept tends to get brought up and reinforced every now and then in various other publications. Basically, it's the Garou, Corax and Nuwisha who are supposed to be <i>really</i> heavily focused on spirit-stuff (and even with the Nuwisha, it's hinted that that wasn't originally intended, but rather mission-creep stemming from the Nuwisha tendency to stick their noses in <i>everything</i> they can).</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent point, and I do agree, it just seems to me to still be more of an oversight than intentional design though, especially in the case of Ananasi. With Nagah I can get that its a part of their ultra secrecy but I feel pretty sure Queen Ananasa would actually need her children to be able to talk to the Triatic spirits. Plus as I said there is player agency to consider too.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T06:13:38-08:00","id":1018040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>deejay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1016420-communing-with-spirits?p=1018001#post1018001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I feel pretty sure Queen Ananasa would actually need her children to be able to talk to the Triatic spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I may ask, why?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>deejay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1016420-communing-with-spirits?p=1018001#post1018001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus as I said there is player agency to consider too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Player agency is going to take precedent over setting. If it makes sense for your game, and it enhances everyone's experience then stepping over a minor setting detail should be a given.<br /> <br /> <br /> Agreeing with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3506_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3506\" data-vbnamecard=\"3506\">Uniform Two Six</a> 's post above.<br /> I would add (imo): Also keep in mind the power level of the spirit will have a lot to do with communication. Spirit Speech is probably required to communicate with most Gafflings (the lowest spirits), while it <i>can</i> (circumstantially) become less and less necessary the higher up the chain you go. I would apply the second half of his/her post into this category. And any higher spirits (Incarna) can certainly understand (and usually makes themselves understood) in most languages. But traditionally you want to address a spirit in it's own &quot;language&quot; and so Spirit Speech is generally a more respectful way to address them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T11:27:30-08:00","id":1018155,"title":"","content":"Isn't it self evident why they would need to, given their tasks? For one thing, they are charged with understanding the Triats original purpose and how it has been twisted. And then correcting that. To that end alone, being able to actually talk to spirits is necessary and desirable. You have to know what a problem is before you can fix it. That's the problem America is in right now - nobody can even agree on the problem, so unity is not feasible and nor is the finding of any solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T11:52:00-08:00","id":1018157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>deejay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1016420-communing-with-spirits?p=1018155#post1018155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't it self evident why they would need to, given their tasks? For one thing, they are charged with understanding the Triats original purpose and how it has been twisted. And then correcting that. To that end alone, being able to actually talk to spirits is necessary and desirable. You have to know what a problem is before you can fix it. That's the problem America is in right now - nobody can even agree on the problem, so unity is not feasible and nor is the finding of any solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't necessarily self evident. The Ananasi don't have to determine what the problem is. Queen Ananasa does that for them. The Queen decides how to go about a solution and sets the Ananasi toward their goals.<br /> <br /> For the record, I am not saying Spirit Speech can't be a helpful Gift. At all. I think there is a decent argument for it being a general Gift for every shifter, Garou included. That being said, I don't think it is inherently <i>necessary</i> for all shifters. It is great to have, but lacking it doesn't bar meaningful interactions with the spirit world. It mostly just means interacting with lower spirits is impossible/difficult.<br /> <br /> I'm going to choose to sidestep the American politics part of that comment. Nothing good comes of real world (especially current) politics on gaming forums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T15:51:52-08:00","id":1018244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1016420-communing-with-spirits?p=1018040#post1018040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...And any higher spirits (Incarna) can certainly understand (and usually makes themselves understood) in most languages...</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh. I think that for Incarna associated with humans in some way (Rat or Cockroach, for instance), that should hold true, but I think it would be weird for Griffon to know any human languages. For Incarna to know the Garou-Tongue makes more sense, I think (a tendency that should become a hard-and-fast law should the Incarna in question happen to be a Garou tribal totem). And actually, I think the distinction of a totem should also be a significant factor. The average raccoon-spirit might not speak the Garou-Tongue, but a specific raccoon-spirit who serves as a pack totem, should. That might also go for human languages. A pack totem of a pack that is made up of all homids who all speak the same (human) language, I could see the totem knowing that language, especially if they (the pack) use it in casual conversation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T01:14:09-08:00","id":1018374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1016420-communing-with-spirits?p=1018157#post1018157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Ananasi don't have to determine what the problem is. Queen Ananasa does that for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disagree with this, for the reason you deemed too sharp and sidestepped - its just not practically workable, and the Queen is not on call 24-7, only in the Sylie. &quot;Know the Great Web for what it is&quot; and &quot;Understand the ways of the Triat both as they were and as they are. Know the difference&quot; are pretty clear directives. The general problem (with spirits) of course is told to them by their Queen from the get go, but the specifics about individual spirits are not supplied, and new spirits are appearing all the time. Secean in particular need to be able to commune with spirits to glean their secrets. This realisation about what is necessary actually comes from playing the game as Ananasi for over 2 years, btw, I am not sitting here blowing smoke just making it up, but hey, your game is obviously different. I am just still very unconvinced that this situation is a design choice. If so, it was a poor one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","user":"deejay","date":". 12-17-2016, 04:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T06:52:12-08:00","id":1018442,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2157_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2157\" data-vbnamecard=\"2157\">deejay</a>, I'm not actually disagreeing with you. Just asking follow questions since that's the only way to get insight into what specifically you think is the problem.<br /> <br /> I suppose my base point is that I don't think it's necessary, though I do see why it is useful. This actually goes for 100% of shifters (some slightly more than others). Being half Spirit, you would think Spirit Speech would be available for everyone. Even the most diehard combat twinked character would benefit from being able to talk to Spirits to help determine who actually needs killing.<br /> <br /> I do think it may have been an oversight. That being said, it is not an insurmountable one. Though that heavily depends on character makeup and playstyles. It could very well be easier to just hand it out than to ST around the lack of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T14:02:39-08:00","id":1018575,"title":"","content":"Yeah I understand, Part of me that thinks it is necessary is also trained to think like a therapist, where the importance of communication in figuring out and solving problems is huge. I have been trying to understand whether or not I have misread the implications and that it was an intentional exclusion, and I wanted to open it up here to see if I had any misunderstandings. I did learn about the Bastet and Rokea, and the Nagah also kinda made sense (they don't want any spirits gossiping about them and aren't part of the pact) which put me on the tracks of thinking I was not seeing something about Ananasi. This is my internal process, and you are helping me with that. I think I am settling on an understanding that this is only a problem with Apis and Ananasi, and that it is up to ST and the needs of the chronicle. My chronicle *needs* spirits, since it is about them, and so it makes sense to involve communication with spirits. Perhaps the default chronicle with Ananasi doesn't really need them, and I am just seeing things through the focus of my playing experience. Or maybe not, and it is a small oversight. It would still feel like a poor design decision, though. Spirits are cool and players should be able to develop close relations with them!<br /> Also, I wasn't trying to stoke any flames with my comparison to the situation in the US, It just seems a genuine simile. Its not even partisan, just an observation that if you cant agree on the problem its almost impossible to find solutions. But anyway, sorry if that was touchy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","user":"deejay","date":". 12-17-2016, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T14:17:23-08:00","id":1018579,"title":"","content":"Personally, I don't think it was necessarily intentional. It may not have even occurred to the writer(s) that it was missing.<br /> For Bastet, what I find amusing is that they don't get the ability to talk to spirits, but as a first rank Gift, the do get the ability to see them. Mind you, Bastet can steal Gifts, so Spirit Speech isn't out of bounds for them. It just isn't something that comes easily. I seem to remember a note somewhere saying Swara had access to Theurge Gifts, which was a tribal secret the other Bastet (Simba in particular) weren't aware of. I'm away form my books though and can't even attempt to look it up. Maybe that was just a house rule my first ST went with.<br /> <br /> I concede your point on the Ananasi. I think any of the shifters who can naturally sidestep probably should be able to communicate with spirits. But again, the necessity of it varies by game.<br /> <br /> I do try and have productive (and hopefully helpful) discourse on here. For the politics thing, it has been my experience that even non partisan politics, especially current events, being discussed has the potential to go downhill very quickly. And so, if it isn't integral to the discussion, I usually just gloss over them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T04:13:02-08:00","id":1020266,"title":"","content":"The Bastet anomaly is amusing. Its like Gaia is encouraging them to poke into other Breeds business. 'Look, spirits! But if you want to learn their secrets, you have to spy on your siblings!' Bastet breed book is where I see that Swara get 'most Theurge Gifts' at an equal rank to Theurges. And yeah Swara like to be underestimated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}